   "design": "Questions, maps and figures live in a tagged item bank from which the paper is assembled. Multiple-choice and map-label items are scored by answer key with item statistics. Essay and analysis answers are grouped by content so the teacher grades each group once and reads every answer; no model proposes scores. The test platform totals marks. Writing questions, colleague review, supervision, grading, registering grades and the inspection session stay with the teacher as appointed examiner.",
   "previous_blocker": "Papers were laid out, scored and totalled by hand.",
   "enabler_now": "Item banks, answer-key scoring and answer grouping.",
   "still_hard": "Map sketches drawn by students.",
   "human_edge": "Seeing whether a student really understands a spatial pattern.",
   "ambition": {
    "kind": "none",
    "what": ""
   },
   "altitude": "Less scoring and totalling; grading judgement stays.",
