   "design": "Students check in by scanning the class code, which writes attendance to the learning platform, so sign-in lists are not typed in. Final grades are published from the gradebook to the student records system by a sync the teacher confirms, instead of entering them twice; fewer transcription errors need correcting. Digital exam papers and forms are archived with the course, and only paper ones are filed by hand. Checking presence, the gradebook, arrangements, administration questions and the exam board stay with the teacher.",
   "previous_blocker": "Attendance and grades were entered twice.",
   "enabler_now": "Code check-in and gradebook-to-records sync.",
   "still_hard": "Paper exams that still need filing.",
   "human_edge": "Handling a student's special arrangement fairly.",
   "ambition": {
    "kind": "none",
    "what": ""
   },
   "altitude": "Less double entry; judgement on arrangements stays.",
